   106	## Shared provider admission
   107	
   108	Provider capacity is owned by `core/provider-process-registry.ts`, independent
   109	of the usage ledger. All Proofbound-owned provider workloads acquire an atomic,
   110	token-owned slot under `.lattice/runtime/provider-process-slots/` before spawn.
   111	Turning off `LATTICE_USAGE_LEDGER` disables usage rows and budget accounting,
   112	not process admission.
   113	
   114	A live recorded pid is never reclaimed because of age. Dead pids are
   115	reclaimable; corrupt/ownerless slots use a bounded stale backstop. Release
   116	checks the acquire token so a late old holder cannot delete a slot that has
   117	already been reclaimed and reassigned.
